     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I didn&#39;t find an entry on this subject: </div><div><br></div><div>I have a simple simultaneous CFA:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;  rskminor =~ h0106.r + h0108.r + h0109.r + h0112.r<br>rskwork =~ h0505.r + h0315.r<br>rskviol =~ h0104.r + h0105.r&quot;</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>I calculate the fit:</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cfa</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>             DF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>             std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lv </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>             estimator </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MLR&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div>I ask for the residuals:</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> resid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;standardized&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div>I get the error message:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"background-color:white;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Fehler in A1 %*% Gamma : nicht passende Argumente&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;error in A1 %*% Gamma: not appropriate arguments&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>No error is generated when the estimator is ML.</div><div>I had a similar problem when running multi group CFA.</div><div><br></div><div>Is this a version but?</div><div><br></div><div>I use lavaan 0.6_1 within RStudio 1.1.423 on a MacBook Pro with macOS High Sierra.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Georg</div></div>"
    ]
